'' A UDT OPERAND IN A NUMERIC EXPRESSION GOES THROUGH ITS OWN 'operator cast'.
'' Measured, over a type that declares 'operator cast( ) as integer' and no comparison
'' operator at all:
''
''     int64 vr$3 = _ZN3UDTcvu7INTEGEREv( &U$0 );
''     RESULT$0 = (boolean)((int64)-(vr$3 != 0ll) != 0ll);
''
'' -- the operator is called and the RESULT is compared. The conversion is what makes
'' the comparison legal in the first place.
''
'' Every one of them declined: the arithmetic path asked the UDT for a value, and a
'' UDT has none. It is asked BEFORE the refusal that stops a UDT reaching that path,
'' because a type that HAS such an operator is exactly the case the refusal must not
'' take. structs/udt-comp-ops-1.bas: 24 -> 0.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/udt-cast-num.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN3UDTcvu7INTEGEREv(@u)
'' GOLDEN: expected/udt-cast-num.out
